WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.120
- [Narrator] This in kombucha.

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.640
Real kombucha.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.850
That iced tea you buy in
those expensive bottles,

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.280
fermented and sweetened?

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.860
It's good, but it's not kombucha.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.080
Somewhere along the line the
word was lost in translation.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.720
In Japanese, "cha" means tea,

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.680
and this is kombu.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.393
This is the story of the real kombucha.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.220
First the kombu.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.270
Kombu is a type of seaweed

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.030
and a staple ingredient
in Japanese cuisine;

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.040
and Rishiri Island, off the
northern most tip of Japan,

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.240
has become known for the
kombu that grows here.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.582
Zenichi Kosaka is a third
generation fisherman.

00:00:39.582 --> 00:00:42.582
(speaking Japanese)

00:01:18.422 --> 00:01:20.220
After kombu is harvested and dried,

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.830
it can be used to make anything from

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.900
soup to salad to garnish,

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.242
but for our purposes,
we're gonna make kombucha.

00:01:27.242 --> 00:01:29.130
Chiharu Hirakawa is a shop owner

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:32.462
selling kombucha from
locally harvested kombu.

00:01:32.462 --> 00:01:35.462
(speaking Japanese)

00:01:46.414 --> 00:01:47.247
I have to ask:

00:01:47.247 --> 00:01:49.475
do you know about American kombucha?

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:51.400
(speaking Japanese)

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.075
Can you guess what it's like?

00:01:53.075 --> 00:01:56.075
(speaking Japanese)

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:03.873
(buzzer buzzing)
Sorry, nope.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.850
But do you have any words for
those seeking real kombucha?

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.850
(speaking Japanese)

00:02:24.905 --> 00:02:27.488
(upbeat music)

00:02:29.651 --> 00:02:32.234
(ringing tone)

